{"id":"PPG_V2.0__compounds__pattern_rename","collection":"PPG_V2.0","category":"compounds","source_path":"PPG_V2.0/compounds/pattern_rename.json","root_names":["PPG::pattern_rename"],"counts":{"nodes":30,"connections":67,"values":19,"overloads":1},"documentation_summary":"Sets PPG face tags for the provided face IDs. Creates a pattern of names from the list in 'Pattern'.","documentation_search":"Pattern Rename Sets PPG face tags for the provided face IDs. Creates a pattern of names from the list in 'Pattern'. Inputs Object Input object Face IDs to Rename An array of face IDs to rename. This can also be a 2-dimensional array. The IDs in each sub-array would get the same pattern name. See 'cluster values' for an example. Inherit Source Tags Adds the name of the source face to the resulting tag name. Pattern A comma-separated list of tags names. If this string is empty then a numeric sequence will be built as the pattern sequence. If the original pattern list contains only ONE element, then this will be used as a prefix for the numeric sequence. Pattern Repeat How to repeat the pattern + Loop: Repeat the pattern in the direction (see Pattern Align) + Bounce: Repeat the pattern forward-backward and skip the first/last element + Bounce+: Repeat the pattern forward-backward and REPEAT the first/last element + Fill: Fill the pattern once and then repeat the last/first element (depending on direction) + Stop: Fill the pattern once and then -1 Pattern Align Sets the direction of the pattern + Start: aligns the pattern left at the start + End: aligns the pattern at the END and fills the array towards the start. Mirror at Center First fills the RIGHT/SECOND half of the resulting array (starting/ending at the center) and then mirrors it over to the LEFT.","port_names":["face_IDs_to_rename","inherit_source_tag","mirror_at_center","object","out_object","pattern","pattern_align","pattern_repeat","reverse_pattern"],"node_types_search":["Core::Array::array_size","Core::Array::build_